# HTTP request collection.
#
# Works with the VS Code REST Client extension and JetBrains HTTP Client.
# Start the service first: `make run`

@base = http://localhost:8000
@apiKey = your-api-key-here

### Liveness -- never depends on the model
GET {{base}}/health

### Readiness -- gates the load balancer
GET {{base}}/ready

### Model identity and live scheduler stats
GET {{base}}/v1/meta

### Prometheus metrics
GET {{base}}/metrics

### Single prediction -- positive
POST {{base}}/v1/predict
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "text": "this service is excellent and works perfectly"
}

### Single prediction -- negative
POST {{base}}/v1/predict
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "text": "absolutely terrible, a complete waste of money"
}

### Batch prediction
POST {{base}}/v1/predict/batch
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "texts": [
    "fantastic quality and fast delivery",
    "broke within a week, very disappointed",
    "does the job, nothing special"
  ]
}

### Client-supplied request id -- echoed back for distributed tracing
POST {{base}}/v1/predict
Content-Type: application/json
X-Request-ID: my-trace-id-12345

{
  "text": "correlate this across services"
}

### With authentication (set api.api_keys or INFERENCE_API_KEYS first)
POST {{base}}/v1/predict
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

{
  "text": "authenticated request"
}

### Validation error -- 422 with the standard envelope
POST {{base}}/v1/predict
Content-Type: application/json

{
}

### Unknown field -- rejected, because schemas use extra="forbid"
POST {{base}}/v1/predict
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "txt": "a typo in the field name"
}

### Whitespace-only input -- rejected rather than scored meaninglessly
POST {{base}}/v1/predict
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "text": "     "
}

### Interactive documentation
GET {{base}}/docs

### OpenAPI schema -- generate clients from this
GET {{base}}/openapi.json
